{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs","id":1273105,"title":"Making a new dog with pieces of two old dogs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-06T08:52:05-08:00","id":1273105,"title":"Making a new dog with pieces of two old dogs","content":"I thought this would be a little too complicated for the ask a simple question topic.<br /> A hypothetical mage has access to death, life, and matter arcana. He has at hand the ghost of a dog, and the corpse of another dog that was killed in a car accident. He acquired the corpse shortly after the accident and using death magic has kept it preserved. Is there any combination of death, life and maybe matter that can put the ghost in the corpse and maybe make a new living dog?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T09:21:32-08:00","id":1273108,"title":"","content":"Death 5 alone would allow you to resurrect the dog and cause the ghost to possess it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T11:02:12-08:00","id":1273116,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Mrmdubois;n1273108]Death 5 alone would allow you to resurrect the dog and cause the ghost to possess it.[/Q<br /> Wouldn't that just result in an otherwise unmotivated living dog being possessed by a ghost? Since animals don't have an issue with souls, I was looking for a way to combine the ghost and corpse into unified living dog. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T11:59:18-08:00","id":1273126,"title":"","content":"You could give the ghost the claim manifestation and make it claim a living dog","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T12:00:26-08:00","id":1273127,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know what you mean by unmotivated living dog, but the dog would be alive and the ghost would get to use it\u2019s body which is as close as ghosts get to being alive most of the time. You could probably cast a Death + Life Patterning Spell to put the ghost in a living body, but in that case you don\u2019t really need the dog corpse. You could still integrate it though if that\u2019s the flavor you\u2019re going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T13:17:42-08:00","id":1273138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273127#post1273127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know what you mean by unmotivated living dog, but the dog would be alive and the ghost would get to use it\u2019s body which is as close as ghosts get to being alive most of the time. You could probably cast a Death + Life Patterning Spell to put the ghost in a living body, but in that case you don\u2019t really need the dog corpse. You could still integrate it though if that\u2019s the flavor you\u2019re going for.</div> </div> </div> </div>By unmotivated living dog, I just meant a dog that was resurrected and didn't have much personality - I know dogs don't have souls as such in COD games, but since resurrected human bodies come back without souls, I assumed dogs came back with little of their original learned traits. Based on RAW, I assume that if you completely resurrect a human body with Death 5, and then attach a soul, the person is completely back (it does not spell that out, but it is the impression I got). Dogs don't have souls, so I thought maybe you could do the same thing by adding a dog ghost.<br /> <br /> Part of the motivation of the mage is that he has worked with the ghost dog for some time and likes him. I know when a spirit or ghost claims a living or dead host, it is not seamless case of body/spirit living in harmony. I wanted to know what was involved in getting the ghost into a dog body in such a way that he is then permanently alive, not a possessing / claiming entity. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T13:23:54-08:00","id":1273140,"title":"","content":"You know Voltaire and Rick Sanchez and what a weird juxtoposition THAT IS, and similar, all talk about how intelligence leads to suffering and alienation to the meaninglessness of life, all life, not just our modern world?<br /> <br /> Ever hear people question if true superintelligent AIs would kill themselves because the burden of intelligence is too philosophically great?<br /> <br /> Lets assume in the Chronicles of Darkness having a soul prevents this. The more intelligent you are, the more you need some spiritual substance to tolerate it, like a soul.<br /> <br /> Dogs don't need souls. I don't think they have souls the way humans do.<br /> (although I would in my game cuz thats depresssing)<br /> <br /> I say your dog can be motivated without a soul but if you use mind to give it human intelligence you'll either see soulloss or it will become a Horror and go mad.<br /> <br /> As for making the dog with arcana less than 5, Im guessing weaving everything but patterning 4 death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T14:24:57-08:00","id":1273146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273138#post1273138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I know dogs don't have souls as such in COD games, but since resurrected human bodies come back without souls, I assumed dogs came back with little of their original learned traits. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there is any reason to make this assumption. Human's come back with no Soul, which does not affect their memories or learned behaviours but will slowly degrade them over time. Dogs never had Souls so would come back exaclty as they left. Although, if there is a dog Spirit that leaves or dies when the dog does that could affect their overall liveliness but not learned behaviour.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T15:22:43-08:00","id":1273159,"title":"","content":"Dunk the ghost of the dog into the underworld river of choice so it becomes a barghest, and then teach it how to use it's new Bargain numina, and your golden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T16:48:43-08:00","id":1273172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs#post1273105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A hypothetical mage has access to death, life, and matter arcana. He has at hand the ghost of a dog, and the corpse of another dog that was killed in a car accident. He acquired the corpse shortly after the accident and using death magic has kept it preserved.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is about two more dead dogs than is Wise to be storing in your fridge, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T20:42:43-08:00","id":1273198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273116#post1273116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that just result in an otherwise unmotivated living dog being possessed by a ghost? Since animals don't have an issue with souls, I was looking for a way to combine the ghost and corpse into unified living dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not a lot of distinction between &quot;ghost-dog possessing a living dog-body&quot; and &quot;resurrected dog with the mind of a different dog&quot; outside of the niche application of Mind to copy the ghost-dog's memories into the live dog-body's brain. Death-savvy characters might be able to spot that this living dog is possessed by the ghost of another dog, but short of destroying one of the two components of this fusion to fuel a spell to make a more concrete combination there's not a lot of ways to accomplish this goal that don't fall short of the specific goal of taking two different dead dogs of different compositions and making them into a third living dog.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273126#post1273126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could give the ghost the claim manifestation and make it claim a living dog</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reasonably certain Claim is conspicuously absent from Mage's copy of the ephemeral being rules for a reason, not least because &quot;possess this thing indefinitely&quot; is accounted for by &quot;Manifestation Conditions instilled by magic last as long as the spell does instead of their normal timespan.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273159#post1273159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunk the ghost of the dog into the underworld river of choice so it becomes a barghest, and then teach it how to use it's new Bargain numina, and your golden.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ghost of a dog is already a barghest, barghests regularly jump right into the River to self-annihilate rather than take the still-ruinous but more measured necessary step of drinking from the waters to become a geist, and not every geist has the Bargain Manifestation, which (besides very probably being out-of-bounds for Awakened magic to grant as a tool for directly creating members of another template) is a means for a ghost to bond with <i>a human</i>\u200b.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T00:09:35-08:00","id":1273234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273198#post1273198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not a lot of distinction between &amp;quot;ghost-dog possessing a living dog-body&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;resurrected dog with the mind of a different dog&amp;quot; outside of the niche application of Mind to copy the ghost-dog's memories into the live dog-body's brain. Death-savvy characters might be able to spot that this living dog is possessed by the ghost of another dog, but short of destroying one of the two components of this fusion to fuel a spell to make a more concrete combination there's not a lot of ways to accomplish this goal that don't fall short of the specific goal of taking two different dead dogs of different compositions and making them into a third living dog.<br /> <br /> I'm reasonably certain Claim is conspicuously absent from Mage's copy of the ephemeral being rules for a reason, not least because &amp;quot;possess this thing indefinitely&amp;quot; is accounted for by &amp;quot;Manifestation Conditions instilled by magic last as long as the spell does instead of their normal timespan.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The ghost of a dog is already a barghest, barghests regularly jump right into the River to self-annihilate rather than take the still-ruinous but more measured necessary step of drinking from the waters to become a geist, and not every geist has the Bargain Manifestation, which (besides very probably being out-of-bounds for Awakened magic to grant as a tool for directly creating members of another template) is a means for a ghost to bond with <i>a human</i>\u200b.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the reason of absence of the claim manifestation is word counting (to make room for the Familiar manifestation).<br /> It s true that the claim would last only until the spell expires, but a master could arrange a indefinite spell.<br /> (Wich could be still dispelled, but the claimed entity would have better attributes than the normal dog, a good but not ideal solution)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T00:26:09-08:00","id":1273235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273138#post1273138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> By unmotivated living dog, I just meant a dog that was resurrected and didn't have much personality - I know dogs don't have souls as such in COD games, but since resurrected human bodies come back without souls, I assumed dogs came back with little of their original learned traits. Based on RAW, I assume that if you completely resurrect a human body with Death 5, and then attach a soul, the person is completely back (it does not spell that out, but it is the impression I got). Dogs don't have souls, so I thought maybe you could do the same thing by adding a dog ghost.<br /> <br /> Part of the motivation of the mage is that he has worked with the ghost dog for some time and likes him. I know when a spirit or ghost claims a living or dead host, it is not seamless case of body/spirit living in harmony. I wanted to know what was involved in getting the ghost into a dog body in such a way that he is then permanently alive, not a possessing / claiming entity. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suggested the claiming instead of possession because the mind of the barghest and the dog would merge, resulting in a &quot;near&quot; normal dog","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T08:45:02-08:00","id":1273446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273235#post1273235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suggested the claiming instead of possession because the mind of the barghest and the dog would merge, resulting in a &quot;near&quot; normal dog</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought claiming invariably resulted in increasingly unnatural changes to the fused being. Maybe I am confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T09:42:13-08:00","id":1273453,"title":"","content":"As described Claimed suppresses the consciousness of the host and have the entity being in charge, not merging both consciousnesses. And yes, it generally adds unnatural physical changes to the host, but mostly because spirits (who are much more likely to use Claim) are quite unnatural. A ghost would make the host seem more like the ghost which means that the resurrected dog would look more like the ghost dog. It might also generate Dread Powers based on the Numina of the ghost dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T11:47:14-08:00","id":1273473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273453#post1273453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As described Claimed suppresses the consciousness of the host and have the entity being in charge, not merging both consciousnesses. And yes, it generally adds unnatural physical changes to the host, but mostly because spirits (who are much more likely to use Claim) are quite unnatural. A ghost would make the host seem more like the ghost which means that the resurrected dog would look more like the ghost dog. It might also generate Dread Powers based on the Numina of the ghost dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true, my wrong on the mind merging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T12:25:29-08:00","id":1273477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273453#post1273453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As described Claimed suppresses the consciousness of the host and have the entity being in charge, not merging both consciousnesses. And yes, it generally adds unnatural physical changes to the host, but mostly because spirits (who are much more likely to use Claim) are quite unnatural. A ghost would make the host seem more like the ghost which means that the resurrected dog would look more like the ghost dog. It might also generate Dread Powers based on the Numina of the ghost dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm wondering, should the mage make the ghost dog his familiar, would the familiar bond survive if the ghost claimed a preserved dog corpse (or a live dog).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T15:06:14-08:00","id":1273502,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Claiming is a fuzzy manifestation. You could have a perfect merging of two disparate entities (In which case you have a third personality that emerges from the other two being suppressed or similar), or you could have one entity being more in control than the other. You could have a Claimed person able to recover from having been Claimed, or the Claiming entity could have done so much damage that the person they Claimed will die without that bond. Mechanically the effects of being Claimed are fairly similar, but exactly how it works and what it looks like narratively will be dependent on the entity that uses the manifestation while always being consistent for that entity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273477#post1273477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm wondering, should the mage make the ghost dog his familiar, would the familiar bond survive if the ghost claimed a preserved dog corpse (or a live dog).</div> </div> </div> </div>'<br /> I don't see why it wouldn't. The Familiar Manifestation isn't disrupted by a spirit also using Fetter or a ghost having Anchors after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T20:24:15-08:00","id":1273653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273198#post1273198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ghost of a dog is already a barghest, barghests regularly jump right into the River to self-annihilate rather than take the still-ruinous but more measured necessary step of drinking from the waters to become a geist, and not every geist has the Bargain Manifestation, which (besides very probably being out-of-bounds for Awakened magic to grant as a tool for directly creating members of another template) is a means for a ghost to bond with <i>a human</i>\u200b.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I haven't read it recently enough. I'd swear it was only a Barghest once it had the bargain, and that animals went into the river more by accident than incident, as they are purely instinctual. Also, geists are specifically rank 3 ghosts with the Bargain manifestation, and they get it by surviving the rivers. Granted, that was from last I read, but again, it's been a while, so I could be wrong here. As far as being out of bounds? Not with death 5- helping a ghost survive a river of death to become more powerful definitely feels like a Master Moros maneuver.<br /> <br /> I also recall that animal ghost use their manifestations instinctively normally, which allows for a the ghost dog to enter the bargain with the dog that it is a ghost of (which is definitely how Scooby Doo survived everything).<br /> <br /> But back on topic! You could absolutely create a dog zombie, then have the ghost claim it, then just maintain it's semblance of life regularly, or just resurrect it while shoving the ghost into it as a soul analogue replacement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T21:22:54-08:00","id":1273658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1273653#post1273653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I haven't read it recently enough. I'd swear it was only a Barghest once it had the bargain, and that animals went into the river more by accident than incident, as they are purely instinctual.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Barghest&quot; is the name for a ghost of an animal. &quot;[They] instinctively enter the Rivers and dissolve into their Plasmic waters&quot; is described as the natural outcome of their entering the Underworld in the absence of a &quot;handler&quot; that can draw their attention away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, geists are specifically rank 3 ghosts with the Bargain manifestation, and they get it by surviving the rivers. </div> </div> </div>Geists are ghosts that have drunk from a River and gained Rank and mobility in exchange for highly limiting their ability to communicate. The changes it wreaks on a geist do not specifically include gaining that Manifestation and the ability to offer the Bargain to a dying mortal is not the defining feature of a ghost who has warped to become emblematic of a form of death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Granted, that was from last I read, but again, it's been a while, so I could be wrong here. As far as being out of bounds? Not with death 5- helping a ghost survive a river of death to become more powerful definitely feels like a Master Moros maneuver. </div> </div> </div>For comparison, the big meta reason Awakened magic can't force an angel to betray its Mission is because that would be giving mages who hadn't crossed the Threshold the ability to make Unchained demons.<br /> <br /> Mage doesn't include Claim on its list of Manifestation Conditions, doesn't allow Awakened magic to raise an ephemeral being's Rank by more than 1, addresses Geister as a subset of Rank 4-5 ghosts, and cannot provide any spell as precedent for &quot;give this entity a Manifestation that allows it to, with no prerequisite Condition, touch a dying mortal to forge an agreement represented by a template on the mortal and a Condition on the geist, both of which only go away when the host dies for good.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not a Master Moros maneuver, that's stuff that archmages fuck around with for an art project.<br /> <br /> It takes a very sideways reading of Mage to interpret &quot;this other gameline uses a nonstandard Manifestation to represent the thing that makes its PCs&quot; as &quot;Mages, who don't even have the more common restricted Manifestation for weird pseudo-permanent merged possession included in their copy of the rules, can't make permanent alterations to the basic makeup of a target with magic, and mathematically can't turn a normal ghost into a geist under their own presentation of what a geist is, can give a ghost the ability to provide themselves as the basis for an indefinite and undispellable gameline-level supernatural template to a mortal character that will last beyond the spell itself.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also recall that animal ghost use their manifestations instinctively normally, which allows for a the ghost dog to enter the bargain with the dog that it is a ghost of (which is definitely how Scooby Doo survived everything). </div> </div> </div>That's\u2026 extremely not how the Bargain works.<br /> <br /> &quot;Make the Bargain with yourself&quot; is only ever speculated to have happened with characters' own Doppelgangers, which are not subject to the same temporal constraints as dying characters themselves on account of being separate entities. Even if a dog had the capacity to receive and accept the offer, it's not getting that offer from its own ghost; the best case is that that ghost might Possess or Claim its own dead body like human ghosts regularly do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T03:41:37-08:00","id":1273699,"title":"","content":"To be fair, it was stated during the Geist 2e development process that having the Bargain Manifestation was what defined a ghost as a Geist. That was changed sometime before the Kickstarter preview. Now the definition is Rank 3+, and does not have to include the Bargain Manifestation. It's commonly achieved by drinking from a River and fluffwise is definitely supposed to be because you drink from the River instead of only being dependent on Rank, but there are some potential situations where it's possible to drink and gain Rank without becoming a Geist (if you only increase to Rank 2) and to gain Rank 3+ without drinking from a River (a Rank 2+ Doppelg\u00e4nger consuming a peer and becoming Rank 3 quite possibly without ever entering the Underworld). I hope these instances are addressed before the final release of Geist 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T07:55:55-08:00","id":1273718,"title":"","content":"They probably won't be, because the rules don't need to address the weird edge cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T08:34:39-08:00","id":1273727,"title":"","content":"I see your point about the former, but Doppelg\u00e4nger who consume their counterparts are extremely likely to be Rank 2. Rank 1 Doppelg\u00e4nger are both unlikely to find another Doppelg\u00e4nger and unlikely to do anything with them, let alone consuming them. It's not a weird edge case when the book specifically includes mechanics for Doppelg\u00e4nger to increase Rank in a unique way and the most common result would be ghosts described to be empowered by the Underworld through mechanics completely unrelated to the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T10:37:23-08:00","id":1273750,"title":"","content":"Just how likely do you think it is that there's a guy running around with a plethora of Dopplegangers? I'd say it's not very likely at all. There are rules for if there happens to be more than one Doppleganger, that in no way suggests that there will be many.<br /> <br /> So Dopplegangers may be likely to be Rank 2...so what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T11:13:18-08:00","id":1273754,"title":"","content":"Plethora while still alive? What? No, you only need one from an NDE and then leave another at the actual death.<br /> <br /> So what? Why include the rule for Doppelg\u00e4nger cannibalism in the first place? Either it's never going to happen and it's a waste of word count, or it's going to happen (because it's narratively interesting) and you'll have to circumvent other rules for it to still fit in the setting.<br /> <br /> A weird edge case is when you apply a rule in a way it's not meant to be applied in the first place or in combination with other rules in an obscure manner. In this case we apply the rule exactly as it is intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T21:40:13-08:00","id":1274136,"title":"","content":"Whoops, didn't see you'd responded <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> <br /> <br /> You know what? I think I completely misunderstood your point about the dopplegangers. Yeah, I could see you getting a rank 3 ghost out of them without them ever visiting the underworld. I don't really see how there's a problem there. I'm also not sure you were indicating there was one, though I assumed you meant there was when you said you hoped the rules would address it. It seems to me though like mechanically it'd be no different than any other Geist coming into existence though naturally the narrative would be a significant departure from the norm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T06:13:35-08:00","id":1274181,"title":"","content":"There's a problem with non-Underworld related Geists as Geists are described as &quot;buried beneath a thick scum of Underworld-tainted Essence&quot;, leave Deathmasks with direct connections to Chthonic Gods when they die, and forget most of their mortal lives (not really an Underworld thing as much as becoming more of yourself by absorbing yourself makes you lose yourself). None of this should hold true for Rank 3-through-ectophagia Doppelg\u00e4nger.<br /> Other Geists are created either through drinking from a River, or as a Guardian Geist at the creation of an Avernian Gate, both events being extremely tied to the Underworld. It makes sense for them to have these Underworld-related effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-13-2018, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T11:19:47-08:00","id":1274222,"title":"","content":"I don't see why it wouldn't continue to hold true, ghosts are themselves very tied to the Underworld, and a doppleganger is absorbing more of that as they cannibalize their fellows and gain in Rank. The rivers are highly concentrated sources of deathly energy, but ghosts themselves, and dopplegangers by extension are also sources of deathly energy, if you imbibe enough of it then it can change your nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T12:34:20-08:00","id":1274237,"title":"","content":"The Underworld is connected to ghosts (specifically, it hungers after them) but I wouldn't assume that holds true in the other direction. Ghosts are generated in the material as psychic echoes by humans, with no known input from the Underworld (other than in the case of Guardian Geists who, naturally, come into being as a Geist). Distance to the closest Avernian Gate does not factor into the plausibility of returning as a ghost, nor do I think that a realm without Avernian Gates (such as a pocket dimension) would prohibit ghosts from generating (though that is admittedly not a common occurrence that it would be required to bring up in Geist, a game that doesn't feature any realms other than the Underworld). It's a relatively common theory that the Underworld is some sort of foreign realm (a Lower Depth in Mage speak) that has latched onto the world and sucks out ghosts like a parasite rather than being a natural extension of the world and natural destination for ghosts. Considering that it's constantly growing it's at least implied it has some sort of beginning. Did ghosts simply not form before that point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T15:18:39-08:00","id":1274258,"title":"","content":"The Underworld isn\u2019t a Lower Depth as it\u2019s tied directly to an arcana. It has been damaged or distorted though, and it\u2019s suffused with a type of energy which ghosts share with it regardless of whether they\u2019ve ever been there or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T15:38:31-08:00","id":1274260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1274258#post1274258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Underworld isn\u2019t a Lower Depth as it\u2019s tied directly to an arcana. It has been damaged or distorted though, and it\u2019s suffused with a type of energy which ghosts share with it regardless of whether they\u2019ve ever been there or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that the Underworld is a Lower Depth, but it's worth remembering that a Lower Depth is a place that is utterly lacking in an aspect of reality, not just one of the Arcana. The place Strix come from lacks Vitae, Duat lacks Sekhem, Denny's lacks supernatural presence, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T17:41:36-08:00","id":1274284,"title":"","content":"As Arcane said, has nothing to do with Arcana (and even if it did there would be 9 other Arcana that could be lacking). Regardless, the theory is that it <i>was</i> a Lower Depth that has latched on, not that it still is one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T17:44:36-08:00","id":1274285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1274181#post1274181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other Geists are created either through drinking from a River, or as a Guardian Geist at the creation of an Avernian Gate, both events being extremely tied to the Underworld. It makes sense for them to have these Underworld-related effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the more prosaic &quot;be a powerful necromancer and die,&quot; but there's a very basic assumption that merits addressing here:<br /> <br /> You can <i>have</i> Rank 3+ ghosts that aren't geists or Reaper-forms. They're often the result of aberrant circumstances and they still won't usually be able to increase their Rank without drinking from a River unless they're a specific exception, but nothing about &quot;Doppelgangers can theoretically reach a Rank above 2 without drinking from the Rivers&quot; implies &quot;Doppelgangers who reach Rank 3 become geists&quot; besides an overly narrow reading of the Ghostly Rank breakdown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T00:36:41-08:00","id":1274324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1273105-making-a-new-dog-with-pieces-of-two-old-dogs?p=1274284#post1274284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Arcane said, has nothing to do with Arcana (and even if it did there would be 9 other Arcana that could be lacking). Regardless, the theory is that it <i>was</i> a Lower Depth that has latched on, not that it still is one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcane wasn't backing you up as much as defining what a Lower Depth is. You'd have to figure out what exactly the Underworld is missing before you could define it as a Lower Depth, and the fact that it does tie to one of the arcana very strongly implies that it's more than just a Lower Depth even if it's function then/now is largely consumptive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}